+// remote_prefill_test: D4 (STRATA_PREFILL_REMOTE_COMPUTE) without a GPU.  Card 1's REAL request path
+// (RemoteExperts::prefill_open / prefill_begin / prefill_end, seabraid::pack_prefill_request) talks over a REAL POSIX shm
+// channel to an in-process expert process running the REAL serve_prefill (plan_prefill_batches, the echo) with a CPU
+// backend: synthetic experts, prefill_reduce_ref (the arithmetic of remote_expert_opt.cu's prefill_reduce_f16), fp16 rows
+// and sums exactly as the wire carries them.
+//
+// What it pins (each sabotaged once and watched to FAIL - see the commit message):
+//   1 sizing    : the prefill region is sized by TOKENS (4H + 8K bytes each, page-rounded), never by pairs
+//   2 equality  : card 1's own picks + the expert process's per-token sums == card 1 computing every pick itself, within
+//                 2e-3 of the token's largest |value| (fp16 rows and fp16 sums: 2 x 2^-11 relative, plus fmaf order)
+//   3 ranges    : a chunk longer than the region goes as several requests; a range with no handed-over pick sends nothing
+//   4 failure   : an error reply or a wrong echo is a failure, and prompt reading on that card is then off (later chunks lend)
+//   5 open      : no region / another width is refused at open, naming both sides
+//   6 model     : the byte/time model computes below its crossover and lends above it
